  "verbalization": "Kaempferol 7-O-rutinoside is implicated in the biological activity of ZR-75-1 through a multi-step mechanism involving integrin beta-1. The drug is directly linked to integrin beta-1, which is a key receptor involved in cell adhesion and signaling. This target is further targeted by (-)-Rosmarinic Acid, a compound that has been shown to interact with integrin beta-1 and ultimately affect ZR-75-1. The evidence suggests a direct and indirect pathway from the drug to ZR-75-1, with the drug acting through a known target and then influencing the downstream signaling pathway. The integration of these pathways supports a plausible mechanism by which Kaempferol 7-O-rutinoside may modulate ZR-75-1 activity. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction between Kaempferol 7-O-rutinoside and ZR-75-1 remains to be fully elucidated.",
